# Patch series for swanstation
#
# Read by scripts/orbis-patch.sh, cmake/OrbisPatch.cmake and the patches CI job. Lines are
# `key: value`; everything after a # is a comment. Patch order is the file name order, which is
# what git format-patch produces and what every consumer here relies on.
#
# upstream/ref name the tree these patches were written against. They are taken from the recipe
# this organisation's CI actually uses, .libretro-super/recipes/linux/cores-linux-x64-generic,
# NOT from the first recipe that mentions the core - the apple recipes pin mupen64plus_next to
# branch `ios` and flycast to libretro's mirror, and a series that recorded those would be
# describing a tree nobody builds.
#
# upstream-status is per patch and is the field that stops a merged patch living here forever:
#   local        ours, not sent anywhere
#   sent <url>   a pull request exists
#   merged <sha> upstream took it; the patch is deletable and a script should say so
# orbis-ports/dynarmic carried six lines for two months after upstream fixed the same defect
# because there was nowhere to write this down.

